Your solution worked perfectly, Stefan. Thanks a lot!In the case of continuous integration within Github as it is the case, it seems we must ask GRASS to be installed in the virtual machine.
This could be done with Stefan's suggestion, adding these lines to the yaml file within .github/workflows:
- name: Install GRASS GIS and other dependencies? ? ? ? run: |? ? ? ? ? sudo apt-get update -qq? ? ? ? ? sudo apt-get install -y -qq grass grass-dev grass-doc wget
You can also see it here:?Install GRASS for CI by ninsbl ? Pull Request #11 ? NINAnor/oneimpact (github.com)
I guess this could be documented for GRASS/R users somewhere? Maybe in some wiki?Any suggestion on where to add this?

BestBernardo

